111
00:13:11,803 --> 00:13:19,150
the corn that's hanging up on the wall there, and much of your Indian corn is all different colors. Sometimes

112
00:13:19,150 --> 00:13:26,170
it's orange and yellow and gold. But once in a while, when you pull the husk down, you find an ear that's

113
00:13:26,170 --> 00:13:33,850
all red. As you know, the Delaware Indians believe that was very good luck. If

114
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:41,490
you found an all red ear, that was good luck. So I think that we should have an ear of red corn to

115
00:13:41,490 --> 00:13:48,610
decorate the homestead. Then you'll notice this is a little broom. We'll be making

116
00:13:48,610 --> 00:13:54,930
these because in the early days the first house you know was a log house.

117
00:13:55,360 --> 00:14:02,840
And there was no wood on the floor, not even any boards. It was a dirt floor. Imagine Mary Miller's

118
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:10,000
problem trying to keep that house clean. It would be rather dusty and dirty, wouldn't it? And so she would make her own broom

119
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:17,400
